A Hacker's Journey
Jon Saxton
April 1991


Jonathan the Priest hasn't been doing too well.  His best effort was many
days ago when he reached level 8 and got annihilated despite having grey
dragon scale mail and Stormbringer.  A bones level was created from that
game but since then he has not managed to get to the eighth level.

Today's story commences with me, Jonathan, once again playing a wimpy priest.
Sure, the chances of getting killed in the early game are very high.  Priests
have limited strength and low-grade armour but they do start off with four
potions of holy water and the ability to distinguish blessed, normal and
cursed items.

Level one, accompanied by Rover provides no challenge.  However in the second
room is a lamp.  Rub.  A puff of smoke emerges.  Adrenalin flows.  Dip that
lamp into one of the potions of holy water.  Rub.  A puff of smoke.  Rub.
Nothing happens.  Rub etc.  Eventually a djinni emerges and grants Jonathan
a wish.  Ponder.  Think back over all the postings regarding what people on
the net consider to be the most valuable item.  Knowing there may be a
Stormbringer and gd scale mail on level 8, I settle for "blessed +3 speed
boots".  Well, I didn't get +3 but I certainly got the speed.

Carrying the lamp in the hope of a recharge Rover and I descend to level 2.
After knocking off a bunch of beasties I'm at experience level 3 having
prayed once to avoid starvation.  I have acquired a small food supply when I
find a couple of potions.  Quaff the white one and everything looks cosmic.
Quaff the cyan one and the world is as dark as the outer cosmos itself.
Bitter experience has taught me to stay as still as possible when blind and
good old Rover was kept busy knocking off the minor nasties which apparently
wandered in.  I had to beat off a couple and managed to hit Rover once myself
although I did not do him a fatal injury.

Eventually vision was restored and after collecting a food ration, a potion
of unholy water and an iridium wand, and knocking off a few more beasties it
was down to level 3.

Level three provided little except a black cap from a passing orc so armour
class was down to 2.  I am now considering the abandonment of Rover but decide
to take him down another level.  Before that happens, however, he meets his
own demise somewhere in the distance.  Oh well, he was a useful ally in my
time of darkness but I only had a sad feeling for a moment, then it passed.
I left level 3 with a second potion of unholy water.

The fourth level yielded a corpse from one of my previous lives.  A vicious
Rover and an intractable ghost were a little difficult to deal with but my
hit points did not dip below 15 and I had a path to flee if necessary.  The
treasures I had left behind were of minor value.  The magic marker was at
least uncursed and the three potions of unholy water were combined with the
two that I was carrying and dipped twice to yield a total of six potions of
holy water.  A nearby room yielded a uranium wand and it was time to start
reading some scrolls.  Just in case one was of the armour-destroying variety
I removed my boots.  Soon I knew about scrolls of teleportation, food de-
tection, magic mapping and identify.  I also knew potions of gain energy,
object detection and restore ability in addition to the elixirs of blindness
and hallucination previously sampled.  I also knew which were the spellbooks
of cure sickness and confuse monster because I had been carrying those
throughout the game but being pretty stupid (as priests are) I had not tried
to transcribe the spells.

At experience level 6 with 40 hit points, I descended to the fifth level.
Among the items in my pack were a cursed and a normal scroll of teleportation
and a scroll of magic mapping.  Not having much use for any of these I stopped
at the first fountain I encountered and dipped them until I had three uncursed
blank scrolls.  The idea was to convert them into scrolls of identify but a
passing fire ant burnt all three scrolls!  Fortunately it didn't do any other
damage.  Meanwhile I had noticed a long sword laying on the ground and with
the idea of converting it to an Excalibur I picked it up and dipped it into
the fountain.  "You have unleashed a water demon."  Oh hell.  "Grateful for
his release he grants you a wish."   Oh holy shit!  "You may wish for an
object.  What do you want?"   Double holy shit!  Stop, Jon.  Think.  You have
a used magic lamp and you don't know how to write charging scrolls, so what
could be more useful than some scrolls of charging?  At this point there is
nothing to lose so I ask for "3 blessed scrolls of charging".  I read one
and my magic lamp glows briefly.  Rub.  Puff of smoke.  Rub.  Djinni appears.
Wishing time again.  What to get?  I still need good armour but I hope I can
pick up a gdsm on level 8.  I have 12 dexterity points so some gauntlets
might be useful.  I have only 9 intelligence points and am too stupid to read
scrolls reliably so a helm of brilliance might be useful.  However my feeling
is that caution is called for.  I still have to get to level 8 and I am not
sure that the bones will be what I hope.  On the assumption that most of the
time in battle I can step back after each thrust I elect to get a good weapon
and opt for Stormbringer, even though I know I might find it cheaply a few
levels further down.  I ask for "A blessed +3 broadsword named Stormbringer"
and I am told that nothing fitting that description is in the game.  I ask
again, leaving off the first "A" and I now hold my favourite weapon.  None
too soon either, because another of those pesky fire ants marches into the
room.  I miss it first time around and I lose one of my charging scrolls and
a couple of potions of holy water.  Second thrust and the ant dies without
leaving a corpse.  A few seconds later another fire ant takes out another of
my bottles of holy water.  Boy, those fire ants are fast!  Time to drop these
potions and my last scroll of charging before they get overheated.

Nymphs have been the scourge of many of my predecessors but now at least they
are easy to deal with.  Hit, step back, hit and nymph is no more but I pick
up a potion of object detection which will eventually become holy water.

A floating eye is on the level but it will take forever to lure it into a
blind alley where I can hack it with impunity.  Fortunately a kobold has left
some darts lying on the ground so a quick trip to fetch those is rewarded
with a floating eye corpse and a "strange sense of acuity".  I abandon my now
useless magic lamp.

Level six.  Still no shops or altars but I figure I'm not doing too badly for
a change.  Actually writing this account helps the game, too, because I have
a tendency to play too quickly and when confronted by nasty monsters often
choose the wrong course of action when a little thought would have yielded
a superior attack or defence.  I'm low on food but a rock mole gets converted
to a cram ration which will help.   Then a dwarf comes by and hit-retreat-hit
tactics yields a precious pick-axe.  Then a red Naga blasts the shit out of
me.  Oops!  I forgot about monsters who can use long-range weapons.  Dead
again.  So much for this story.

==============================================================================

15th April, many dead priests later .....

Taxes are done and there's nothing better to do at the moment so after a few
quick deaths, Jonathan the Priest is on level one again having just killed
enough beasties to push his experience level to two when he finds a pair of
hiking boots.  He puts them on and is told "You feel yourself speed up".
Hooley dooley!  It really is a full moon today!

Down to level 2 carrying the usual armour (plus the speed boots), weaponry,
literature and drinks together with a low-powered magic marker (35).  A
scroll called JUYED AWK YACC in the entrance turns out to be cursed.

A few more monsters meet their doom and Jonathan reaches experience level 3
then 4 before descending to level 3.

A floating eye is found in one of the rooms but Rover seems to have vanished
so the eye is lured into a blind alley.  I hate dealing with these things -
so much can go wrong - but I'm now trapped.  Rover appears and kills the eye
but it doesn't leave a corpse.  Still at experience level 4, I make for the
downward stairs.  I still want to take Rover with me and find that wearing
speed boots is actually a DISADVANTAGE for that exercise.  Rover only takes
one step for every two of mine and I'm getting hungry.  I remove my boots and
eat a clove of garlic and things are more normal.  A gecko along the way 
provides further nourishment.

On level four I don my speed boots again.  I don't hear any shopkeepers so I
drop all my gold at the top of the stairs.  Mistake.  On the other side of
the dungeon Manlobbi is keeping shop and amongst his wares is a cursed lamp
and an uncursed one.  The cursed lamp is interesting; could that be a magic
lamp?  I scuttle back to the stairs to retrieve my gold consuming the last
of my food on the way.  I know Manlobbi has some edibles for sale and with
my charm I know he won't charge too much for an eat-in meal.  I figure that
is better than calling upon Cron when near starvation.

Just for fun I pick up the uncursed lamp and #rub it.  Shock! Horror! Oh no!
A bloody djinni appears and grumbles "It's about time!"  The UNCURSED lamp
was magic and I missed the chance for a wish!  Wait, what about the cursed
one?  Sure enough it too is a magic lamp.  There is yet hope.  Purchase both
lamps, have another bite to eat and exit the shop, #dip the cursed lamp twice
into my holy water and finally #rub it.  Wish for 3 blessed scrolls of
charging.  Pooh!  Only got one.  Recharge lamp, #rub and wish for a blessed
+3 gray dragon scale mail.  (I hate spelling "grey" as "gray" but I get what
I ask for.)  Armour class is now -6.  Sell the lamp back to Manlobbi and keep
the half-used one for the day when I get or write another scroll of charging
(I still have my magic marker!).

Up to previous level to get rid of Rover and to #dip my cursed JUYED AWK YACC
into a fountain.  I can't afford to treat the lamp yet - I need more potions
which I can convert to holy water so I can enchant my marker or the blank
scrolls and with only two potions of holy water left I have to be a bit con-
servative.

Back to level four and then on down to level 5.  I'm hoping to encounter a
dwarf now so I can get a pick-axe.  In a little room there is an altar to
Mitra and a blessed scroll called JUYED AWK YACC.  Dare I read it?  Yes.
Mistake.  It is a scroll of fire and my scroll of blank paper burns.  Damn.
Still, it could have been worse.  I might have lost my holy water as well,
although here I have the means to generate more.

On level 6 I find a potion which turns out to be one of monster dectection.
There seems to be a dwarf here.  Another scroll improves the light.  The
dwarf corpse turns into a food ration and I retrieve the pick-axe.  Quickly
back up to level 4 to rob Manlobbi.  I dig a tunnel around the corner of
his shop and through the wall and start kicking goodies out of the shop.
A dwarf enters and leaves me a pick axe in his will - a bit late for me.
There are some potions in the shop so I dig a pit outside, fall through and
climb back to level four again.  Soon there will be some frustrated Kops.

Oops, I forgot.  A while ago I ate a snake and felt healthy.  I was just
reminded because a snake bit me and its poisonous bite was ineffectual.

Grabbing all the potions I fall through my prepared trapdoor to level 5 and
toss up whether to convert the potions to holy water or to identify them.
Choosing to identify them I put myself in a little blind alley in case I
lose my sight.  A purple potion lifts me into the air; an ebony potion speeds
me up and a brown one gives me hives.  Hmm, none of those was useful; they
could all have been better used as water.

Back on level 6 I am grateful for poison resistance because I get bitten by
a quasit several times.  After beating my way out of a dust vortex I am at
experience level 7 with 44 hit points.  I throw a bunch of darts (gathered
from a kobold some time ago) at a floating eye and experience a strange
mental acuity when I gobble the corpse.  A brown pudding rotted my speed
boots and I have a couple of scrolls.  I am scared to read them in case one
of them destroys some of my armour.  What I'd really like is to find a book-
shop.

Level 7 looks suspicious.  Something has been eating its way through walls.
Yes, someone has been here before.  Just outside Ackhalataki's armour shop
is a pile of useless junk left behind by a ghost who has apparently been
sent to its final destiny.  Well maybe it isn't all useless - the cursed mud
boots might just let me walk on water and the cursed plate mail is sold
several times until Ackhalataki runs out of money.  Along another path one of
my ghosts delivers some more useful stuff - including six potions of unholy
water which will soon become holy. An opera hood turns out to be a cloak of
protection so my armour class is now at -7.  Up to level 5 to that lawful
altar to convert the unholy water without sacrificing my two existing potions
of holy water.  To reduce the weight of my pack a little I #dip the magic
lamp now, rather than later.  Back down to 7 again but while still on 5 I
acquire teleport abilty by eating a leprechaun corpse.  From the second pile
I pick up a cursed scroll of light and go looking for a fountain.  There isn't
one so it is back up to level five yet again!  #Dip the scroll and it is
cursed, blank.  #Dip it into holy water and it is uncursed.  #Dip the magic
marker and write a scroll of charging.  Charge the lamp and #rub it.  Djinni
grants me a wish!  Stormbringer please!

Now I have speed, good armour, and a fine weapon.  I am at level five but
I have been to level 7.  I know that level 8 has some good stuff but I don't
think I'm going to need it.  I have three scrolls unidentified and I am
scared to read them.  I park myself in a blind alley, remove all my armour
and put on the cursed mud boots.  Read HACKEM MUCHE and my boots disintegrate!
Whew!  What if I had been wearing GOOD stuff?  Now it is OK to put armour on
again.  I am still wielding my mace but none of my scrolls is cursed so I can
afford to wield Stormbringer.  VE FORBREDERNE makes me feel materially poor.
VENZAR BORGAVVE makes my hands glow red.  Nothing very useful there.  I still
haven't seen a scroll of identify!

Back on level 7 a white potion makes me blind for a long time.  I try hitting
a blue jelly but have to be careful as my hit points rapidly decline.  Even-
tually I do beat the jelly to death but its corpse turns into a potion which
I cannot immediately identify.  I take a peek downstairs to see what monsters
await me on level 8 but return quickly to known territory.

So here I am on level 7 with a good chance of meeting myself on level 8.  I
have good armour, a powerful weapon and I am fast and healthy.  However I
have lousy personal attributes: just 52 hit points max, poor strength and
dexterity at 10 and 9 respectively, reasonable constitution at 15, low intel-
ligence at 10, I am wise at 18 but my charm is just 10.  I am temporarily
blind.  My progress will not be easy.  This is a critical stage of the game
and calls for maximum care.

There is a white unicorn nearby which kicks me occasionally.  Maybe I can
do something useful with it.  I acquire a unicorn horn but I am not sure if
I can safely eat the corpse so I leave it alone.  I seem to remember adverse
effects from eating unicorns - does it make Cron angry?  Cannot afford to
take the risk at this stage.  I have no food and might need to be rescued
from starvation.

After getting some nourishment by hunting a jaguar I regain my sight and the
potion I picked up earlier proves to be water.  It is now time to explore
level 8.

I note that I am still carrying the magic lamp.  It is now useless so I drop
it, gathering instead a potion of blindness.  A cockatrice falls to the good
old hack-and-back tactics but I have no gloves so using the corpse as a
weapon is out of the question.  I hope I don't get blinded and teleported to
the site of the corpse!  No sign of a ghost yet but after swatting a car-
nivorous ape I gain another experience level.  I am now at 9 with a maximum
of 62 hit points.  There is a dog in the room but I suspect it is not Rover
because I never have a pet accompany me this far.  It is just an unnamed dog
but it is not vicious so I leave it alone.  A locked chest is kicked open
and yields just a cursed bubbly potion.  Pressing keys too quickly I hit a
floating eye by mistake but fortunately it dies immediately.  What if I had
been frozen by its gaze?  Goodbye, probably.  Eating the corpse blinds me
for a while but I note that the cockatrice corpse has vanished so there is
no immediate risk from that quarter.  Well, level 8 held nothing of interest
after all.  Strange.  I don't think anyone else has been here.  I've come
down one more level but have not made any gains in terms of abilities.  I
had a narrow escape with that floating eye.  That should be a warning to be
even MORE careful as I descend to level 9.

Three killer bees and a bunch of mordor orcs are quickly disposed of but
leave nothing very valuable behind.  I left a swag of gold on the previous
level - perhaps I should fetch it and leave it near the top of the stairs
on this level?  While up that way I get hungry and derive insufficient
nourishment from the edible beasts which come my way.  I am forced to pray
to Cron for sustenance but I am carrying a unicorn horn and I know that it
can be used for something.  On the assumption that a blessed unicorn horn
is better than a normal one I #dip it into holy water but I do not test its
properties just now.  I have to go up two levels to fetch my 8000+ gold and
progress is erratic because of my uncontrolled teleports but eventually I
get back to level 9 and drop the gold at the top of the stairs.  Gold is
generally pretty useless stuff and I don't like carrying it but should I
find a priestess soon then I have a chance to buy some protection fairly
cheaply at only 3600 per point.

A jaguar provides immediate nourishment and a lembas wafer will satisfy a
future appetite.  Meanwhile a random teleport takes me to a fountain where
the potion of blindness is converted to water.  Another teleport to another
fountain.  I #dip the cursed bubbly potion and the water glows for a moment
before the fountain dries up.  Test the potion?  Yes.  It tastes like liquid
fire so I call it grog (that's Australian for booze).

The random teleports are becoming annoying and I hope I find a tengu soon.

Spellbooks abound but I am too stupid to read them so I don't bother carrying
them around.  I recall that one of the piles back on level 7 had a cursed
harp.  I am a long way from the castle level but I worry about not being
able to open the front door.  Still, I figure by then I should be able to
level-teleport back to 7 if necessary.  I don't have the strength to carry
too much.  There is a cursed pair of fencing gloves here and I wonder if
they might just happen to be gauntlets of power....

Meanwhile there are sounds of crashing rock.  And I left all that gold at
the top of the stairs.  I hope it isn't a rock mole!  No, it turns out to
be a dwarf king and he is carring the gold rather than eating it.  On level
10 I drop the gold (now over 9000 pieces) at the top of the stairs again.
A chest yields nothing but another spellbook of detect monsters which I
leave there.  At this point I am carrying

	Weapons
	  o - a blessed wide sword named Stormbringer (weapon in hand).
	Armor
	  b - a +1 cloak of protection (being worn).
	  j - a -1 pair of speed boots (being worn).
	  p - a cursed pair of fencing gloves.
	  u - a +0 visored helmet (being worn).
	  x - a blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail (being worn).
	Comestibles
	  s - a lembas wafer.
	  t - a food ration.
	Scrolls
	  q - a scroll of light.
	  r - a scroll labeled TEMOV.
	Potions
	  d - 2 potions of holy water.
	  e - 2 potions of water.
	Rings
	  l - a ruby ring.
	  m - a cursed ivory ring.
	Wands
	  f - a marble wand.
	  i - a cursed glass wand.
	  k - a cursed wand of sleep.
	  v - an oak wand.
	  S - a wand of sleep.
	Tools
	  a - a blessed unicorn horn.
	  h - a blessed magic marker (24).
	  H - a pick-axe.

Not too shabby for strength 10!

Wearing one -1 piece of armour I am reluctant to try on the gloves just now
but I feel compelled to risk reading TEMOV.  (My only real worry now is a
scroll of punishment but scrolls of identify and enchant armour/weapon are
much more common and I haven't seen any of those yet.)  Well TEMOV makes
Stormbringer glow blue for a moment.  Interesting but not really useful.
Identify or enchant armour would have been better.

Three more scrolls are found, ANDOVA BEGARIN (bendover again?), a cursed
scroll of gold detection and LEP GEX VEN ZEA.  Hmm.  Read ANDOVA and it
shows me a map.  Not useful.  LEP turns out to be a scroll of identify and
my ruby ring offers fire resistance.  (I hope I don't have to rely on the
ring for that.)  I have two scrolls which I can now convert to identify
other things but water is in fairly short supply.

On the way to the stairs a passing long worm provides a none-too-nourishing
meal and leaves a potion of speed.  Fountains!  Where are they?

On level 11 I find the downward stairs and drop the gold.  I am becoming
concerned about fire-breathing monsters now so I leave the water and holy
water there too for now.  A bugbear leaves behind some minor nourishment in
the form of a couple of fortune cookies and a pancake.  A fountain here
lets me wash a couple of scrolls so now I have a cursed and an uncursed
blank.  In the process the fountain overflows and creates a lot of puddles
but I can't walk on water so I cannot use them.  Level 11 turns out to be
quite small and not much is happening there so I descend to level 12, find
the stairs again and drop the same stuff once more.  There's a sink here
but I don't have any duplicate rings so I go exploring.  After encountering
what seems to be a blind alley I am touched by a ghost which eventually
succumbs to my battering.  Oh what a pile of goodies!

	a potion of unholy water
	2 cursed food rations
	a brass wand
	a cursed puce potion
	a cursed scroll labeled VELOX NEB
	a cursed sky blue potion
	a cursed gray dragon scale mail
	a blessed pair of riding gloves
	a cursed gold ring
	a cursed rusty pot
	a cursed lock pick
	a cursed magic marker
	3 blessed scrolls of blank paper
	a cursed tin wand
	a cursed scroll of charging
	a cursed hexagonal wand
	a war hammer named Mjollnir
	2 cursed gray stones
	a cursed oak wand
	a cursed agate ring
	a cursed scroll labeled ELAM EBOW
	a cursed magic marker
	a cursed faded pall
	a cursed pair of speed boots
	a cursed pick-axe
	5 cursed scrolls of blank paper
	a cursed pair of mud boots
	a cursed silver ring
	a knight corpse named Sam

Mjollnir!!!!  (But can I carry it?  Probably not.)  Lots of blank scrolls
including three blessed ones.  What about the grey (gray) stones?  Two of
them?  Surely they are luckstones?!!

The mud boots are likely to be water-walking shoes.  First lets try the
blessed riding gloves....they turn out to be +4 gauntlets of dexterity!
I consider the rusty pot; after all, the visored helmet I am wearing doesn't
seem to have any special attributes.  Go on!  Iit may be cursed but I can
be fairly sure it won't have a negative defence properties. Remove and drop
the visored helmet, pick up and wear the rusty pot ... well my intelligence
didn't change so it isn't a helm of brilliance.  I don't see any monsters
close by so it may not be a helm of telepathy but it certainly doesn't have
a negative armour class, it is +4!  Now I think about those cursed speed
boots.  If Sam had been enchanting armour so much I wonder if the cursed
boots in the pile are better than the uncursed -1 boots I am wearing.  What
is there to lose?  Not a lot.  Go for it!  +3!  Now my armour class is -20!

OK.  Time to take stock.  I am still short of water so I gather the cursed
potions from the pile.  I hate to leave Mjollnir behind in case some beast
picks it up and hits me with it.  That would indeed be rude beyond belief!
Somehow I am able to pick it up without getting a message saying that I am
having difficulty!  A bug in Nethack?  I seem to have a lot of stuff for my
10 points of strength.

Moving off the pile of goodies a quivering blob pops into view in the near
distance - in a nearby room.  So that rusty pot I am wearing is indeed a
helm of telepathy.  Great!  That will be very useful on the Medusa level
and in the castle and it means that I don't have to be quite so careful
about monsters with long-range effects.

Twice I encounter a succubus who kindly removes all my armour.  After the
second episode I wander naked (risky!) back to the pile where I am tempted to
try out Sam's grey dragon scale mail.  It may be cursed but chances are it
won't be worse than mine.  Not at all!  It is +6!  The succubus has damaged
me somewhat.  My constitution is down to 13 and my wisdom down to 17.  Still,
that shouldn't be a major tragedy.  I want to know about those mud boots.
If they are for walking on water then I have the means to acquire some much-
needed holy water.  There is some risk in investigating because I'll use up
my magic marker but I note that Sam left one and surely it coulnd't be any
worse than my lousy 34-point one!  Gather the blank scrolls, write a blessed
scroll of identify.  I get to know about quite a few things.  The fencing
gloves I've been carrying for a while are gauntlets of fumbling.  The mud
boots are indeed water-walking boots, Sam's faded pall turned out to be a
cloak of invisibility and my ivory ring was found to cause aggravation.
There is a lot more to be identified here but the most immediate need is for
more holy water.  I dress appropriately, drop my useless cloak, gloves and
ring and head upstairs.  On the way I find another (cursed) copper ring and
stop to drop it in the sink.  I am told "You hear the ring bouncing down
the drainpipe".  Not very informative.  Maybe a ring of hunger?

Back at the pools I decide that holy water is more important than identifying
the various potions so I #dip everything and finish up with six potions of
holy water and one of unholy water.  I use up my marker writing a scroll of
identify and head back down to the pile.  The copper ring does indeed prove
to be hunger but the gold is regeneration.

I drop my own magic marker and pick up Sam's.  I have a couple of blessed
scrolls of blank paper left so I just uncurse Sam's marker and write another
scroll of identify.  There are two of them - I hadn't noticed before.  After
that the first of Sam's old markers shows as having just one charge left,
the other one (still cursed) has 20.  I have a cursed scroll of charging
which will take 2 potions of holy water to convert.  Which magic marker do
I charge?  Not mine, so I'll try Sam's uncursed one.  Unfortunately the
marker was permanently dried out.  Oh well, maybe I can identify some wands.
The brass ones turn out to be wands of light so I abandon them for a moment.
I find a level teleporter here but I stay on this level because I am wearing
magic-resistant armour (gdsm).  I have two oak wands - one cursed and one
uncursed.  When I try engraving with the cursed wand, I discover that I have
two wands of wishing!  Un-bloody-believable!  So what do I want from these?
More than anything else, some blessed potions of gain ability.  Lots of them!
Unfortunately the wands of wishing yield only cursed potions of gain ability
so I am going to have to convert them.  I suspect I have made a bad mistake
because I am carrying the two grey stones and they are cursed.  Oh well, no
great tragedy.  Maybe I can recharge the second wand later on.

You are not going to believe this.  One wand made my engraving disappear.  I
didn't know whether this indicated a wand of teleportation, cancellation or
invisibility so I dropped a couple of cursed blank scrolls and zapped the
wand at them.  The scrolls disappeared but they were not invisible so I went
looking for them.  I have now encountered yet another pile of goodies left
behind by someone else's corpse!  Presumably Sam had disposed of the ghost
because it was nowhere around.  Among the treasures are a bunch of potions.
Most are cursed but a few potions of water aren't.  A trip to the pool leaves
me holding 11 potions of holy water!  2 are used to bless the potions of gain
ability whereupon my characteristics become somewhat more respectable.
Strength is 14, dexterity is 13 (boosted by the gauntlets to 17), consti-
tution is at 17, intelligence is at 14, wisdom is maximum at 18 and charisma
is a reasonable 14.  I #dip my water-walking boots so I can remove them and
put on my speed boots.  Armour class is now -23.  Not too bad!  The grey
stones hold a blessing so I strongly suspect they really are luckstones.

Oops!  Pressing keys too quickly again I mistakenly attack a nymph and she
steals my cloak of protection!  Then the stupid woman steps onto the level
teleporter!  AAAARRRGGGHHHH!

I go on a scroll-collecting excursion.  I find the two blank scrolls I
teleported earlier and pick up the remaining four from the first pile.  The
second pile yields a few more and I finish up with nine.  I #dip the scrolls
to uncurse them, pick up the uncursed magic marker from the second pile and
#dip that.  After writing blessed scrolls of charging and identify I have a
50-point blessed magic marker and eight blank scrolls left.  Now - about that
wand of wishing .... WHERE IS IT?  I no longer have it!  Surely that bloody
nymph didn't get it too?  Seems like she did!

What chance the nymph teleported upwards?  Only about 20% but it is cheap to
look.  On level 8 FOOBIE BLETCH causes me to forget the layout.  No problem.
All the way up to level 1 but, as expected, no sign of the naughty nymph.
Much sustenance is provided by all the cream pies those Kops are carrying
but there is nothing worth reporting.  I did manage to score some more
holy water by playing around on level 7.  Now, after uncursing my speed
boots I have six.  I still have plenty of blank scrolls.  A couple of stone
giant corpses boost my strength to 16.  I wear my ring of regeneration to
consume food quickly!  Back on level 12 I collect a bunch of cursed rings
and write blessed scrolls of identify.  I find a ring of conflict and of
polymorph control but I do not succeed in identifying them all.  What is
more, my magic marker won't recharge.  I thought those things could be re-
charged indefinitely?  Perhaps not.  There's a cursed magic marker with
20 points left in it in a pile so I pick that up and bless it.  I create
yet another blessed scroll of charging which again fails to revitalize the
magic marker.  What a waste!

On level 13 a blessed PRATYAVAYAH uncurses everything in my pack.  I remem-
ber that I have left 10000+ in gold on level 12 so skip upstairs to fetch
it.  Back on level 13 I drop quickly to 14 to dump the gold.  Level 14 is
in the old hack style without ANSI graphics.  Level 13 provides nothing
further of interest, neither does 14.  On 15 I drop the gold and soon dis-
cover a room full of dead things.  For this lot I wield Mjollnir instead
of Stormbringer.  By the way, Mjollnir is +3, Stormbringer is +4.

Played too quickly again!  Beat up a wraith and jumped on the corpse to
eat it.  Didn't pay enough attention to the message at the top of the
screen.  The wraith didn't leave a corpse and I started munching on a human
corpse.  Big mistake.  I am told "You cannibal!  You will regret this!"

Meanwhile I am solicited by a nurse.  I retreat to a blind corridor before
undressing but I have another random teleport before much happens  I en-
counter the nurse again near a doorway and I get my hit points up to 74
before the nurse leaves.  Meanwhile a nymph is hovering around, just visible
through the doorway.  I dress quickly then use the hack-and-back technique
on her.  I step onto the site of her death and, guess what!  There is the
wand of wishing I lost earlier.  Of course I no longer have any scroll of
charging, nor a magic marker with which to make one.  Sigh!

After eating a couple of woodland elf corpses I feel wide awake.  A couple
of quick encounters with the nurse push my hit points to 78 but then I fall
through a trapdoor to level 17.  Careful, Jon.  There is a blue jelly here
and my hit points drop precipitously as I try to convert it to a corpse in
the hope of gaining intrinsic cold resistance.  I retreat and put on my ring
of regeneration before returning.  Before I manage to clobber the blue jelly
it does something I've never seen before.  Apparently the heat of my body
made the jelly divide!  The clone left a corpse but eating the corpse was
unproductive.  Meanwhile my helm of telepathy shows a rust monster lurking
in the vicinity.  I suspect I don't have any rust resistance so I opt to
leave it alone.  Maybe a wand would deal with it?  I zap it with a wand of
cancellation but I am not sure if that takes away its propensity to corrode
armour and weapons so I hit it with a sleep ray as well.  A sky blue potion
makes me confused as I climb up to level 16.

I hear dice being thrown.  I presume there is a barracks on this level.
Sure enough, a random teleport takes me there and I dispense with the
soldiers and some other beasties which wander in to participate in the
fighting.  My only reward is some food and a blessed +4 ring of protection
which doesn't overly excite me.

Up on level 15 again to collect the gold I notice a brown pudding wandering
around.  I manage to avoid it while having fun with the nurse and my hit
points rise to 81.   

The gold is too much to carry all at once so I have to make three trips to
deposit it at level 18.  I hope all this is worthwhile.  I have only seen one
altar so far and certainly no priestess.  Level 18 is being eaten to bits
by an umber hulk but he is no match for me.  At the far end of the level I
bump into a blank square which quickly succumbs to Mjollnir.  Yet another
pile of goodies.

	Things that are here:

	a cursed long sword named Excalibur
	2 cursed scrolls of teleportation
	a cursed plumed hat
	a cursed small shield
	a cursed pair of padded gloves
	a cursed gray dragon scale mail
	a cursed scroll labeled NR 9
	a cursed pick-axe
	a cursed war hammer
	a cursed ring of polymorph control
	a cursed pair of hard shoes
	a cursed scroll of blank paper
	a cursed magic lamp
	a cursed wand of polymorph
	an iron wand
	9 potions of unholy water
	a cursed ring of adornment
	a cursed gem called white glass
	a cursed wand of undead turning
	an ebony wand
	a cursed wand of cancellation
	a cursed iron wand
	a cursed scroll of blank paper
	a cursed wand of teleportation
	a cursed uranium wand
	a cursed ring of regeneration
	a cursed balsa wand
	a silver wand
	a cursed long sword named Demonbane
	a cursed iron wand

You'll note that I left out the exclamation mark at the end of the previous
sentence.  You see, although this is a great treasure, there's not much here
that I really need.  Even the magic lamp is of little interest.  Presumably
it has been used once and there is no scroll of charging available.  It is
interesting that there is a war hammer here.  What is the betting that it
was once Mjollnir until Sam wished for a war hammer by that name?  The nine
potions of unholy water might prove worthwhile and I can convert them if I
can first get two potions of ordinary water.  You see, the problem I have is
that I am carrying just one potion of holy water but I need two to convert
all the unholy water to holy.  I have one potion of ordinary water so if I
can get another I can use my holy water to enchant the two ordinary ones
and then use those to bless the unholy potions.  I am also carrying some
other potions, namely sickness, speed and blindness, none of which I need
so on a quest for a fountain to convert one of my useless potions to water
I drop to level 19.  I find a fountain but it dries up after only one #dip
so I don't succeed in diluting my potion of sickness enough.  I do find a
blessed scroll of remove curse which would be sufficient to help me convert
the unholy water but I also find a Priestess guarding an altar to Set.  By
sacrificing a few killer bees which were buzzing around the altar is quickly
converted to my alignment and now I have another means to get holy water.
I drop a bunch of stuff and return to level 18 to collect those nine potions,
bring them back to the altar, drop them to make them into ordinary water and
use my holy water to enchant the whole ten.

On the way I have discovered a potion of gain energy and I have eaten a
gelatinous cube to gain cold resistance.  I am wearing my ring of teleport
control to suppress the random excursions since there is a reasonable supply
of food around.  I still have that unicorn horn too.  Maybe I should try it
out and see what it does?  Nothing happens.

While I am looking at the pile of stuff back on 18 I realize that there was
another solution to the holy water problem.  I am carrying a wand of can-
cellation and could have zapped it at the unholy water.  I might just try
zapping the whole pile anyway.  It will be interesting to see what happens
to the artefacts.

First let me identify some wands.  Engraving with a curved wand riddles the
ground with bullet holes so I call it "magic missile".  A uranium wand
unsuccessfully fights my attempt to write so I call it "striking".  A cursed
balsa wand produces no apparent effect except that I thought I engraved
"eewq" but the message on the ground reads "2ewq".  Curious.  Did I make a
mistake?  Did the cursed nature of the wand produce a bad engraving?  Anyway
the wand isn't a wand of nothing because I have identified those; neither is
it a wand of locking for the same reason.  I conclude that it is probably a
wand of secret door dectection, probing or opening.  I zap the wand and it
is directional so it isn't secret door detection.  I zap a closed door and
nothing happens so I suspect it is probing.  Sure enough, I zap it at myself
and I am told my stats.  A silver wand proves to be a wand of digging.  An
ebony wand makes the bugs on the ground speed up so I zap that one at myself
but it glows violently and turns to dust.  An iron wand proves to be a wand
of cold and that is the lot.  I try zapping the wand of cancellation at the
pile and observe that everything becomes uncursed and the artefacts retain
their names.  Just for fun I turn the wand of cancellation on the pile of
wands that I have made and I learn something, namely that the wands all lose
their charges, and in fact show -1.  This alerts me to a probable mistake on
my part.  The cursed magic lamp in the pile probably had a charge left and
I've most likely killed it forever.  Oh well!  Discovering things is what
hack is all about.

I gather my holy water and carrying as much gold as possible descend to the
temple level and offer the priestess 4400 gold pieces.  I am rewarded with
a change in intrinsic armour class from 10 to 6.  Up on the previous level
to fetch more gold once more I am the victim of my own folly.  I beat up
a soldier, step on the pile of things he leaves behind, note that there is
a C ration, quickly type e and then y.  Oops!  The soldier left a corpse.
"You cannibal!  You will regret this!"  I guess it is time to appease the
gods somehow.  Fortunately a golden naga corpse from the next level down
seems to do the trick!

A second offering to the priestess gives one more point of decreased armour
class but I haven't enough gold for a third so I drop it just outside the
temple and descend again to level 20 where a couple of hill orcs immediately
attack me.  Since I am close, I carry the corpses back up to the temple and
sacrifice them on the altar.  The first gives me a glimpse of a four-leaf
clover, the second gives me Fire Brand which is not really useful.  I still
hope to get intrinsic fire resistance before I go to hell.

I've tried applying the unicorn horn a couple of times but "nothing happens"
so I am not sure what it is for.

I quaff a glowing potion and everything looks cosmic.  Back on 20 I can hear
the footsteps of a guard and a little exploration with the pick-axe reveals
a vault.  There's not quite enough gold for two donations to the temple but
I get one more armour class decrement.

I'm now having a lot of trouble carrying all the useful stuff I collected so
I make two trips to get all the goodies down to level 21 after leaving the
surplus gold on 19.  21 yields another temple, this time dedicated to Cron.
Pity I left all my gold back on 19!  Still, I take the opportunity to drop
Fire Brand in the temple on 19 because I have noticed that monsters tend
not to enter the temples.  Back on 21 and no longer hallucinating I manage
to tempt a grey dragon into the temple by leaving gold around but I cannot
get it to stay on the altar so I just leave the gold in the temple, leave
the many blank scrolls and potions of holy water that I am carrying on that
level and descend to 22 to see if there is anything interesting.

Well the first thing I do is step onto a level teleport trap.  That is handy
to know.  Then an inscription on the floor leads me to suspect that there
might be a vault on the level so I investigate, only to discover a second
level teleporter just a few steps away from the first!  I notice that my
movements on this level are a bit sluggish and I suspect there might be
a beehive or other large collection of beasts.  Sure enough, a passing
sergeant leaves behind a potion of monster detection which reveals a huge
beehive near where I entered the level.  Good.  I can use the extra
strength which I expect to get from eating the royal jelly.  A nymph came
out of nowhere and stole a wand of sleep but no great tragedy; I'll deal
with her later (so long as she keeps off those level teleporters).

At the entrance to the beehive I put on my ring of regeneration because I
am going to need to be hungry.  Although I have a ring of conflict I don't
bother with it.  I figure I can deal with the bees more quickly myself and
that does indeed prove to be the case.  Bees do not stand up to a single
blow from Mjollnir and my hit points do not waver below the 83 maximum.  A
couple of other creatures attack me from behind but they do not last long.

Now into the hive with all that royal jelly!

Trouble is I still have no appetite so I decide to grab the 1200 gold pieces
lying around and visit the temple again on the previous level.  That together
with what I had left there before reduced my intrinsic armour class to 3
although I had to give 4800 pieces of gold this time.  Back down to 22 to
munch on a few royal jellies and my strength is up to 18/04 before it is
time to go on a further calorie-consuming excursion.  This time I drop down
to level 23 laden with stuff which I will probably discard later.  While
there I find a vault with enough gold for another visit to the temple so
after playfully dispatching three guards who got angry just because I would
not drop the gold I dug my way out and climbed up two levels to #chat to
the priest of Cron.  With intrinsic AC now at 2 wearing all my good armour
gives me -30 and if I put on my ring of protection I can get -34.  I still
have no intrinsic teleport control and no intrinsic fire resistance.  I see
a tengu while digging my way out of the vault but it leaves no corpse.

I think I know what a unicorn horn does.  I went blind from eating a lump
of royal jelly and having nothing better to do applied the horn and found
that I could see again.  Of course that is not conclusive, I could have
regained my sight naturally.

After swallowing as many royal jellies as I could stomach I gathered the rest
and headed downstairs.  At level 23 I guess I can expect to encounter Medusa
fairly soon.  I have no blindfold but there is a potion of blindness in my
pile of stuff which I carry in shifts down the levels.

I find a bunch of gold, not quite enough to buy another AC decrement in the
temple but fiddling around on level 22 I notice a mummy wandering around in
a tiny area and I hear the footsteps of a guard.  More money!  I dig my way
into the vault.  Lots of gold!  With the rest which I have cached I should
get two favours.  Damn, not quite.  Still, all these tunnelings and excur-
sions are using up food, of which I have a surfiet.

A wraith on level 22 fails to yield a corpse.  I am still only at experience
level 12 which is a bit lower than I'd like.  On level 23 I eat my fill of
royal jelly, pushing my strength up to 18/19, remove my ring of regeneration,
pick up as much as I can carry and drop down to 24 to start transferring my
goodies deeper into the dungeon.  On 24 I deliberately approach a yellow
light (in case this is the medusa level) and when blinded see a room full of
dead things across the other side of the dungeon.  Maybe I can eat some
wraith corpses?

There were five wraiths but only one left a corpse.  There are a lot of
chests to open but first I go exploring and encounter a blessed magenta
potion which I quaff and gain permanent invisibility.  An inscription on
the floor leads to another level teleporter.  There are six chests in the
graveyard but the only thing of vague interest is a cursed dark blue
spellbook.

Oops!  A lich just cursed me!  He got my holy water.  Damn!  It is a long
climb up to a lawful altar.  Never mind, there are plenty of level tele-
porters around so getting up is easy.  I can't remember where the altar is
so I go all the way up to level 3 and find one there.  On the way back I
stop off on level 7 to pick up the cursed harp because I have yet no way
to enter the castle via the front door.  Further down I find a wraith which
leaves a corpse so I reach experience level 14 and I also read a bunch of
spellbooks which I couldn't have read before.  A red naga leaves a corpse
but I don't get any intrinsic fire resistance from it.  Maybe I'll have to
wait for a red dragon for that.  One other thing I could really use is a
means to levitate.  A ring would suffice and would be lighter to carry
than a pair of boots.  I know a spell of levitation and that may be enough
to deal with the castle level but I don't know that I am intelligent enough
to cast it.  An emerald ring which I have been carrying doesn't lift me off
the ground so I am probably going to throw it away.

Back at level 23 I get swallowed by an ochre jelly.  As I beat my way out
I am splashed with acid and I am told that my gauntlets are not affected
and my war hammer named Mjollnir is not affected.  Hmm, interesting.  It
looks like they are already rustproof.

I'm getting hungry and I only have a couple of pancakes left which don't
provide a lot of nourishment.  On my way through level 24 I see a blue
dragon so I'll go back and eat it.  It blinds me but Stormbringer makes
quick work and although I have a hard time eating it all, I am rewarded
with amplified health.  I guess that means I am now shock resistant.

I go down the stairs to drop some stuff and have a look at what is there.
It is not the Medusa level because all I can see is a priest of Set and
a dwarf.  The dwarf is busy hacking out the level.  I find a wire ring but
that doesn't give me a lift either.  I'm not interested in rings of poly-
morph and I can't think of any that I might want other than levitation so
my plan is to leave the inidentified rings behind.  I'm having enough
trouble carrying things as it is.

Returning briefly to level 24 I clobber a winter wolf, pick up a mirror and
the rest of my gear and move down to 25.  There isn't much of interest here
and I have nothing to say to the priest of Set.  I must be quite close to
the Medusa level now so before descending to level 26 I check my pile.  What
happened to the potion of blindness?  Surely I was not so stupid as to con-
vert that one to holy water?  No, of course not.  I wonder.  I scuttle up
through the levels looking at every pile of stuff.  Thank Cron, I find it
on level 19.  Without it I'd have had a real problem in dealing with the
lady of the writhing snakes.

(To be continued ...)

